# Strobes Shell Bridge Agent Configuration
# Copy to .env and fill in your values

# Required
STROBES_URL=https://app.strobes.co
STROBES_API_KEY=your-api-key-here
STROBES_ORG_ID=your-org-uuid-here

# Optional
# STROBES_BRIDGE_ID=auto-generated-if-not-set
# STROBES_SHELL_NAME=my-server
# STROBES_CWD=/home/user
# STROBES_VERBOSE=true

# --- Sandbox pack (pre-installed security tools + Python runtime) ---
# The pack (nmap, nuclei + nuclei-templates, httpx, ffuf, gobuster, subfinder, dnsx and
# a full Python with boto3/reportlab/curl_cffi/cryptography) ships INSIDE the artifact:
# baked into the Docker image and embedded in the standalone binary — nothing to install,
# no runtime download, works offline. These are optional overrides only:
# STROBES_PACK_DISABLE=1                               # ignore the pack; use only host tools
# STROBES_PACK_PATH=/opt/strobes-pack/linux-x86_64    # point at a specific pre-extracted pack
# STROBES_PACK_URL=https://github.com/strobes-co/strobes-bridge/releases/download/v0.1.0
#                                                     # base URL to fetch/auto-update the pack from
#                                                     # (a release that carries the pack tarballs)

# --- Auto-update ---
# The platform tells each bridge on connect what agent/pack version it should be running
# and the bridge updates itself "when required": it re-pulls the sandbox pack in place
# (needs STROBES_PACK_URL) and, if it is the standalone binary, swaps + relaunches itself.
# STROBES_AGENT_URL=https://github.com/strobes-co/strobes-bridge/releases/download/v0.1.0
#                                                     # base URL to fetch a newer agent binary from
# STROBES_NO_SELF_UPDATE=1                            # refuse binary self-update on this host

# --- Network egress scope ---
# Every command the bridge runs is confined by the OS (Seatbelt on macOS,
# bubblewrap on Linux) so its only route out is the bridge's egress proxy, which
# applies the policy below. A tool that ignores proxy settings therefore gets no
# network rather than unfiltered access.
#
# The bridge starts OPEN: with nothing set, commands reach anything. Listing any
# allow entry switches it to default-deny, so only what you list is reachable.
# The platform can also push scope at runtime (sandbox_configure), which
# overrides these and takes effect on the next connection.
# STROBES_NET_ALLOW=api.example.com,10.0.0.0/8   # hostnames, IPs or CIDRs
# STROBES_NET_DENY=10.1.0.0/16                   # deny always wins over allow
# STROBES_NET_DEFAULT=deny                       # traffic no rule matched (default: allow)
# STROBES_NET_BLOCK_METADATA=0                   # allow 169.254.169.254 (default: blocked)
